  "text_md": "Reading: Kim Assignment:\n\nFinalize paper topic, begin outline\n\n# October 23: International structure and levels of analysis\n\nReading: Waltz\n\n# October 24: International structure and levels of analysis (continued)\n\nReading: Waltz\n\nAssignment: Brief paper outline\n\n# October 25: The intersection between domestic and international relations\n\nReading: Gourevitch Reading: Putnam\n\nReading: Chung\n\nReading: Chung\n\n# October 26: Conclusion of the course\n\nAssignment: Detailed paper outline and presentation\n\n# October 27: In-Class Final Exam\n\n# November 10: Final paper due on Canvas at midnight CST\n\n# Assignments, Grading and Due Dates:\n\n# Class Participation:\n\nStudents must read the assigned material before engaging in discussion and must contribute as much as possible to the in-class discussions. Each student is likely to find considerable benefit in the exchange of ideas, doubts, and criticisms during discussions. Much of the value of a graduate class is in the sharing of the knowledge and perspective that each participant brings to the sessions.\n\n# Final Exam:\n\nA final exam will be distributed during the final class session. The exam will cover all readings assigned for the class, as well as material discussed in class.    \n\n# Analytical Paper:\n\nStudents will prepare an analytical paper about an international topic of their choice. The paper will model an outstanding form of analytical writing as discussed in class. It will be 5-7 pages (double-spaced) and will examine and evaluate a contemporary international issue from a particular theoretical perspective and level of analysis. The final paper will be due on November 10 via Canvas.  \n\n# Grading:\n\nThis is a letter-graded course: A, B, C, D, or F. The standard grade scale will apply: 90%-100% = A; 80%-89% = B; 70%-79% = C; 60%-69% = D; below 60% = F.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Assignment  </th>\n    <th>Percent of Grade  </th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Class Participation</td>\n    <td>20%</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Analytical Paper</td>\n    <td>40%</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Final Exam</td>\n    <td>40%</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nNotice: Failure to meet assignment due dates could result in a grade of I (Incomplete) and may adversely impact Tuition Assistance and/or Financial Aid.\n\n",
